  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Which graph correctly shows the solution to the inequality \( \dfrac{7x-3}9 \geq
            8-2x \)? Show or explain your reasoning.</para>

          <para>A</para>
          <figure class="unnumbered">
            <media
              alt="A number line is shown. There is an open circle on 3. The number line to the right of 3 is highlighted.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_14_01.svg" />
            </media>
          


          <para>B</para>
          <figure class="unnumbered">
            <media
              alt="A number line is shown. There is an open circle on 3. The number line to the left of 3 is highlighted.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_14_02.svg" />
            </media>
          


          <para>C</para>
          <figure class="unnumbered">
            <media
              alt="A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on 3. The number line to the right of 3 is highlighted.&#10;">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_14_03.svg" />
            </media>
          


          <para>D</para>
          <figure class="unnumbered">
            <media
              alt="A number line is shown. There is a closed circle on 3. The number line to the left of 3 is highlighted.">
              <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_14_04.svg" />
            </media>
          
        </problem>
        
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer: Your answers may vary, but here are some samples. Graph C.</para>
          <list>
            <item>I tested 2, 3, and 4 for the values of \(x\), and 3 and 4 make the inequality
              true.</item>
            <item>I solved a related equation and then tested a couple of values on either side of
              the solution.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
    </section>
  </content>
